              "text": "Where you can order a birthday cake online depends on your location, budget, and how quickly you need it. \n\n### 1. Nationwide Delivery (U.S.)\nIf you want to order a gourmet or famous cake and have it shipped directly to your door (often flash-frozen with dry ice to keep it fresh), these are the top services:\n\n*   **Goldbelly:** This is an online food marketplace that curates and ships food from the most famous bakeries across the United States. You can order iconic cakes from places like **Carlo's Bakery** (*Cake Boss*), **Lady M** (famous for crepe cakes), **We Take the Cake**, and more. \n*   **Milk Bar:** Famous for its signature, nostalgia-infused \"B'Day Cake\"\u2014a three-tiered vanilla cake with rainbow sprinkles, chocolate crumbs, and vanilla frosting. They ship nationwide and offer gluten-free options.\n*   **Magnolia Bakery:** Known for its classic, retro-style American buttercream birthday cakes (and world-famous banana pudding).\n*   **Bake Me A Wish!:** The go-to option if you need reliable, next-day nationwide delivery. They specialize in classic, beautiful birthday cakes (chocolate, red velvet, carrot cake) and have excellent customer service for gifting.\n*   **Harry & David:** Great for high-quality classic cakes, cheesecakes (including selections from *The Cheesecake Factory*), and gift baskets.\n\n### 2. Same-Day or Local Delivery (U.S.)\nIf you need a cake **today** or tomorrow, nationwide shipping won't work. Instead, use local delivery services to bring a fresh cake from a nearby bakery or grocery store:\n\n*   **Instacart or Shipt:** Use these to order from local grocery stores (such as Whole Foods, Publix, Kroger, Wegmans, or HEB). Grocery store bakeries are highly reliable, budget-friendly, and can write custom messages on the cake.\n*   **DoorDash, Uber Eats, or Grubhub:** Search \"bakery\" or \"cake\" on these apps. They will connect you to local, independent bakeries in your neighborhood that can deliver a cake to your door in under an hour.\n\n### 3. Nationwide Delivery (UK)\nIf you or the recipient are located in the United Kingdom, there are fantastic online cake delivery services that specialize in postal cakes:\n\n*   **Cutter & Squidge:** Famous for all-natural, incredibly beautiful birthday cakes, brownies, and afternoon tea boxes delivered across the UK.\n*   **Lola\u2019s Cupcakes:** Offers stunning handcrafted birthday cakes and cupcakes. They offer hand-delivery in London and select surrounding areas. \n*   **Patisserie Valerie:** A classic choice for luxury, handmade celebration cakes with next-day UK shipping.\n*   **Bakerdays:** Excellent for personalized photo cakes and custom designs with quick next-day delivery.\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips for Ordering Cakes Online:\n*   **Lead Time:** For nationwide shipping (like Milk Bar or Goldbelly), try to order **at least 3 to 5 days in advance** to secure your preferred delivery date.\n*   **Defrosting Time:** Most nationwide shipped cakes arrive frozen or cold-packed. They typically require 2 to 12 hours in the refrigerator or at room temperature to thaw before they are ready to serve. \n*   **Allergies:** If you need gluten-free, vegan, or nut-free options, bakeries like *Milk Bar* (gluten-free) or specialized local bakeries on *Instacart/Uber Eats* are your best bet.",
